shape = SubResource("Shape_floor")

; --- the house ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Composed by `python tools/compose_building.py ashfall_house 3 4 1 --hollow`. Its own scene carries
; the per-wall colliders, the open doorway and the floor at y = 0, so it needs nothing here but a
; position. ⚠️ Under `Nav`, so its walls carve the bake and nothing paths through the house.

[node name="House" parent="Nav" instance=ExtResource("7_house")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, -6)

; --- interior light -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ⚠️ A ROOF KILLS THE SUN AND THE ROOM GOES BLACK. The chandelier and the wall lantern are meshes;
; neither emits anything. These two Omnis are what makes the interior readable, and the only way to
; know they are needed — or that they are enough — is to render from inside.

